    <h2>The Irresistible Crackle of Candy Shells in Cold Cream</h2>
  <p>The culinary magic of the M&amp;M's® Milk Chocolate Blizzard relies on a unique physical phenomenon: candy shells chill instantly to freezing temperatures, creating a crisp, brittle crackle before giving way to smooth milk chocolate centers. While soft bakery mix-ins like dough or brownies blend into a homogenous consistency, M&amp;M's retain distinct crunchy pockets throughout the entire cup. At 490 calories for a Small and starting at $3.49, it provides an energetic burst of color and crunch. Discover every candy creation across <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>M&amp;M's Blizzard vs. Other Candy-Bar Blizzards</h2>
  <p>The M&amp;M's Blizzard sits in the "candy-bar Blizzard" tier alongside Butterfinger®, Snickers®, and Heath®. All are priced at $3.49 Mini / $4.49 Small. The key differences:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>M&amp;M's</strong> — Crunchy candy shell, milk chocolate center. Visually colorful. Best for those who want the classic M&amp;M's crunch in a frozen format.</li>
    <li><a href="/items/butterfinger-blizzard"><strong>Butterfinger®</strong></a> — Crispy, peanut-butter wafer pieces. Lighter in flavor.</li>
    <li><a href="/items/snickers-blizzard"><strong>Snickers®</strong></a> — Nougat, caramel, peanut pieces. More complex texture.</li>
    <li><strong>Heath®</strong> — Toffee and almond. Distinctive buttery crunch.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>A Vibrant Hit for Families &amp; Younger Guests</h2>
  <p>With its cheerful kaleidoscope of red, yellow, blue, and green candies suspended in creamy white soft serve, this Blizzard is consistently the #1 requested treat among kids and teens. If ordering family value bundles like the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> or a <a href="/categories/kids-meals">DQ Kids Meal</a>, upgrading to or adding a Mini M&amp;M's cup ($3.49) guarantees an instant celebration.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
